 a step-by-step guide
This workshop guide will take you through the process of repairing a wooden chair. The guide is designed to be easy to follow, and the steps are written in a way that is clear and concise. The guide includes diagrams and photos to help illustrate the process and make it easier to understand.
Step 1: Assess the Damage
The first step in repairing a wooden chair is to assess the damage. This will help you to determine what needs to be done to fix the chair and what materials you will need to complete the repair.

To assess the damage, look at the chair carefully and identify any areas that are damaged or worn out. This may include loose joints, broken legs, or damaged wood. Take notes and photographs to document the damage so you can refer back to them later.

Step 2: Disassemble the Chair
Once you have assessed the damage, the next step is to disassemble the chair. This will give you access to the various components of the chair